    "title_en": "Recent developments in particle flow calorimetry-a snapshot",
    "abstract_en": "The Particle Flow Paradigm is a driver for most if not all detector concepts for current and future colliders. There are several approaches to implement particle flow in detectors. These include a high three-dimensional segmentation or the emphasis on measuring subcomponents of jets with high precision. This article reviews briefly the status of the various approaches mainly based on material shown at the LCWS2025 in Valencia.",
